Q: I created an object with `Object.create(null)`, then reassigned the variable. Why does the object have a toString property now? A: <p>With the following line, you're recreating an object:</p>

<pre><code> ages = {Boris : 29, Liang : 22, &gt; Julia : 62};
</code></pre>

<p>What you wanna do is the following I suppose:</p>

<pre><code> ages = Object.create(null); 
 ages.Boris = 29;
 ages.Liang = 22;
 ages.Julia = 62;
 console.log("Do we know toString's age?", 'toString' in ages); // =&gt; false
</code></pre>

<p>Regards,
Vincent</p>
